---
// T064 — price-comparison value-anchor per 01-STRATEGIC-DOCTRINE.md
// §7 Bet #3: "€15/month single tier is 3-5x below per-sim coaching
// (€80-150/hr human coach)." The comparison is honest math: a year
// of LAP at €150 equals roughly 1-2 hours of human coaching depending
// on the coach's rate.
//
// Copy respects 01-STRATEGIC-DOCTRINE.md §3 anti-persona ("Pro
// drivers with dedicated coaches → we are not trying to replace
// Driver61") — closes with the explicit "not a replacement" clause
// so readers who already have a coach see LAP as additive rather
// than displacing, and readers considering a coach understand LAP
// is not a substitute.

const HEADING_ID = 'pricing-value-anchor-heading';
---

<section
  aria-labelledby={HEADING_ID}
  class="px-grid-margin border-steel/10 mx-auto mt-24 w-full max-w-6xl border-t pt-24 sm:mt-32 sm:pt-32"
>
  <article class="mx-auto flex max-w-2xl flex-col">
    <p class="text-steel text-caption tracking-wide uppercase">By comparison</p>
    <h2 id={HEADING_ID} class="font-display text-h2 text-chalk tracking-display mt-4 text-balance">
      A year of LAP is one hour with a human coach, or two.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-steel text-body leading-body mt-6">
      Per-hour sim coaching runs €80 to €150 depending on who you book. A year of LAP at €150 —
      every session captured, every drill prescribed, every outcome checked against your baseline —
      costs roughly what one hour of coaching costs.
    </p>
    <p class="text-steel text-body leading-body mt-4">
      LAP is not a replacement for a human coach; it is the always-on layer underneath. If you
      already work with a coach, LAP gives them the data; if you don&rsquo;t, LAP is the daily
      practice log that makes hiring one worth it later.
    </p>
  </article>
</section>
